#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096493 :question/id #uuid "6dfe09f0-30e2-53bc-a8f6-d7e4a3b8232a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5181" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3042242136b82b867b8bd7911761ee38318924df0c9979488d20f04117c45d9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf a$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/b3/b316448c885a20a7ed60871ce0f1a4dc4f77bd4658dc6eda3407fb3c89a088cb.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\angle AHB = 90^\\circ\n$$\n\n, $AH=3$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^{2} + BH^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$ is $\\sqrt{13}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{\\mid a \\mid} \\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b11642dd-80cc-539c-8c2d-8cdee58e9d3e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049923 :topic/id #uuid "1ed8dd8d-e728-5e57-81fe-a7c1a6a08469" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124481} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124482} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124483}] :topic/math-academy-id 1927 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048132} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048702} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048868} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048952} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049029} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049067} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049878} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049999} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050341} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050496}] :topic/title "The Product Rule for Radicals"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050315 :topic/id #uuid "3f453bac-6f10-55b6-9795-7cf9ac76659e" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138394} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138395} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138396}] :topic/math-academy-id 2240 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048428} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048868} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048952} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049067} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050887}] :topic/title "The Quotient Rule for Radicals"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565626 :question-generator/id #uuid "7368cb97-d918-59db-bc60-953954990dde" :question-generator/script "generators/d0/d0a64c548406081439b9e9f013975dfcfe53858d534f986ac7f9fe87af01eb59/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae96c78f-e10d-563b-82af-e2c02160928e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094940} {:answer/id #uuid "25f7a90e-939a-568d-ba3d-07a616fcb021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{q + r}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094941} {:answer/id #uuid "328e6ad2-ef2f-5827-8881-60cdfaebb76b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2q}{\\sqrt{13}} + \\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094942} {:answer/id #uuid "681555fa-cdb3-5281-b943-0cf1eed80c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(q + r))/(\\sqrt{73})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094943} {:answer/id #uuid "703e463a-8826-5adf-9d3d-36bfd8037d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{q + r}{\\sqrt{13}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "681555fa-cdb3-5281-b943-0cf1eed80c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(q + r))/(\\sqrt{73})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094943} :answer-field/id #uuid "96962338-e491-50f7-b8da-1efc8b69ba83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094939}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d05ca0e-131b-5294-8367-1760396e4369" :question/math-academy-id "q-19276" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9dfaf74a497a2fd22428e09a4c26d573e184c9728ccf67f11ebb9d6a2a44f4c6.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $q + r$?" :question/worked-solution "The scale shows that two grid squares represent one unit. Reading the displacements from the diagram gives\n\n$$\nq=\\left\\langle\\frac52,-\\frac32\\right\\rangle,\n\\qquad r=\\left\\langle\\frac32,3\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nThus $q+r=\\langle4,\\frac32\\rangle$ and\n\n$$\n|q+r|=\\sqrt{4^2+\\left(\\frac32\\right)^2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}2.\n$$\n\nThe required unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\frac{q+r}{|q+r|}=\\frac{2(q+r)}{\\sqrt{73}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8688d259-91a0-57b9-a118-ec71feec2112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{65}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095036} {:answer/id #uuid "a1324d04-e706-5a76-a501-88a91adb3e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{55}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095037} {:answer/id #uuid "228bdee3-07e5-5a7d-9a23-1d3da2c66da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095038} {:answer/id #uuid "44ddca2e-c35f-567f-9191-68cb552e7650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{55}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095039} {:answer/id #uuid "4741a424-03b7-5a24-97e3-1e5c43226795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{65}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4741a424-03b7-5a24-97e3-1e5c43226795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{65}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095040} :answer-field/id #uuid "943eaa96-2961-5fec-9654-295f42c3d887" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095035}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ddbfd9c-fd49-551e-8c5c-9bdbb0fc04fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-20407" :question/problem "![](images/13/1319298a994d5daf26853baf7d255490827ada4123debdf0b4374db1ed03f7af.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$." :question/worked-solution "The scale shows that two grid squares represent one unit. The vector moves four grid squares right and seven down, so\n\n$$\nc=\\left\\langle2,-\\frac72\\right\\rangle,\n\\qquad |c|=\\sqrt{2^2+\\left(-\\frac72\\right)^2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}2.\n$$\n\nDividing by the magnitude gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{|c|}=\\frac{2c}{\\sqrt{65}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bf6d318-67a3-589f-aa06-712a4c979552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512262} {:answer/id #uuid "5466b133-5ea5-525f-8cd7-1a549d321d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512288} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9a8734-2fa1-5cd5-97d6-c6ffcae6ba4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512426} {:answer/id #uuid "9b35183a-e748-54ed-8dd3-0bcbe740b891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512466} {:answer/id #uuid "ed844729-fa98-5650-835d-6732a8a4b167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b35183a-e748-54ed-8dd3-0bcbe740b891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512466} :answer-field/id #uuid "5749cf60-a3f1-5876-9c2b-03d5d66464f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512772}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "45f48cf6-e519-5407-abc6-4bbd59c8789a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119805" :question/problem "![](images/95/95c30eab094a24beb6976262167401efa973dbac12781c69d074eb14e12e2743.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{m}+\\mathbf{n}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n:$ \n\n![](images/87/87647211f77776c5f5f740c205fafb150eef1b9d3ebefb82df73a9fdcd953bdb.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=0.5=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $BH=2.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|m+n| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}(m+n).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a455916-32b4-5125-a03d-acadaf8f7915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{10}}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502359} {:answer/id #uuid "74dbaa7e-fca7-5073-a877-6b16ff3e4d78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502367} {:answer/id #uuid "8a06c96f-4a15-5bf2-a6d0-edbdb248951e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502372} {:answer/id #uuid "90fb3517-b11c-5317-ac7d-17e978e3d179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502376} {:answer/id #uuid "c45caa27-da31-57ac-8666-1a0bb5c8d193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c45caa27-da31-57ac-8666-1a0bb5c8d193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502404} :answer-field/id #uuid "139bd750-f127-56f4-9c8c-dad3ecb6aa91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502330}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "15405bfd-218a-5ebb-ac44-be3eba615aca" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d62b7f63213e0a36a4cc186c396de6986f8c9e594fa045791d9c37fad7550f60.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m+n$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n$:\n\n![](images/ae/ae31ae08afde8173954eef7609108f51e2a5113e7ef37a815511d29e653f33bf.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=0.5$ and $BH=1.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{9}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5}(m+n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44542f74-71e7-507c-ba2a-4a28f636ac89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{5}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502352} {:answer/id #uuid "57d39e45-b7dc-5b05-accd-6ded543fb154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502357} {:answer/id #uuid "c55ad23b-68a1-557a-aa55-3f07c42db8a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502405} {:answer/id #uuid "e16574a4-34e8-54cf-a77e-3ad1ef0fe437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502420} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b27dcd-fc04-5048-9e40-7aa9d5043980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e16574a4-34e8-54cf-a77e-3ad1ef0fe437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502420} :answer-field/id #uuid "94d9330f-8252-5b46-9c3b-ad958ccbb399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502378}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25059bd6-40b8-5009-96b3-70ae023f7607" :question/problem "![](images/35/35ce1ab5c1689dca152c58e955e4a43c0be0e2bc6a796bf20e84f2c99786f8ca.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/9b/9b906579f40ce2a1c59129d80540b339c1bb00fcd9a5f5ce179b01efeb702ab5.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=3.5$ and $BH=0.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $c$ is $\\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|c|}\\cdot c \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aeab7be-8c7d-5a3a-be9f-120546db36cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{17}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502337} {:answer/id #uuid "78dffdfd-3b80-57ec-a318-d95ddef548d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502369} {:answer/id #uuid "b21b2119-51aa-5753-ab74-53f404fe7b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502390} {:answer/id #uuid "c0949ae1-36a1-539c-9ddd-694612a88e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502402} {:answer/id #uuid "dc94450a-5a6d-5d38-bd5d-47e15a6a879e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{17}}{17}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78dffdfd-3b80-57ec-a318-d95ddef548d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502369} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf6beda-d9da-55d2-92ef-7c06f8adde74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502423}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e59a005-0b33-5ed7-ad5d-fc08843b1882" :question/problem "![](images/11/1112fef974be645940a11f8f3f099ca6b0125a6a92ca8642712dde7b86c63ac8.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/4c/4c8930d8535e42d793def554d8e65943e637c02debb6d411048096ba1b8cda68.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=2$ and $BH=0.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(2)^2+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $c$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|c|}\\cdot c \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d788b6-d7d5-53f9-baa9-94394f07c1f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502346} {:answer/id #uuid "3ac393dd-d1cc-54b8-bd96-c686fc1523d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{109}}{109}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502348} {:answer/id #uuid "5612fc05-2875-50ee-bed6-ce8a32dc5501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{109}}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502355} {:answer/id #uuid "b70bf890-655a-5da2-bb16-078c7a660b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{109}}{109}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502395} {:answer/id #uuid "e29a47d6-0232-5e4f-87d6-8ea17544ebfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{109}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ac393dd-d1cc-54b8-bd96-c686fc1523d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{109}}{109}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502348} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5db592a-0691-5283-a627-c1c5c2ea250f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502394}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "570883a2-63cb-5ec8-886b-b501a7b97685" :question/problem "![](images/36/364b9ef322e1d6c1aaa54e23a2c09bf086f3721370da7b69aa7036222d1e4318.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m+n$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n$:\n\n![](images/89/894f70223b9b29220ee424f53c1ae82ff804fc9b7ca3638e43481d7cea63f66a.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=5$ and $BH=1.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(5)^2+\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25+\\frac{9}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{109}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{109}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{109}}{109}(m+n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10044cc3-3b39-5d32-a498-68916d941200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{13}}{13}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502329} {:answer/id #uuid "17c2381b-c4e7-5a02-b1bd-1af3ad2fe815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{13}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502336} {:answer/id #uuid "33b225c1-7ac2-59b0-87c8-2d938ed0e64c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{13}}{13}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502345} {:answer/id #uuid "b3420529-9ac1-56ba-9621-898ba6e04a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502392} {:answer/id #uuid "becfdc1d-6591-5de1-83cf-85a6a6e00bc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10044cc3-3b39-5d32-a498-68916d941200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{13}}{13}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502329} :answer-field/id #uuid "431eaaa1-c585-54de-bea0-dfe869377d08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/t