a$ is $5$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1466a4c6-98a6-5c4f-ae70-75f167118229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502333} {:answer/id #uuid "643d241c-b09e-5d13-be8a-2f780530c24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{53}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502361} {:answer/id #uuid "aa33eb03-a7ce-5a51-a4de-b374da32635c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502382} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e4d2ac-8630-5990-b322-df632250a0ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{106}}{53}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502389} {:answer/id #uuid "ed10a18f-9c1f-56ec-b6f6-99a8b4f36321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{53}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed10a18f-9c1f-56ec-b6f6-99a8b4f36321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{53}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502424} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b0da6b-7675-58cf-9104-1d77abf27492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502419}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "be9bc2f6-f852-5ff9-bd62-113bf0a7214a" :question/problem "![](images/13/1313a6787b3d2da5ddf917ad9cad72791bc465a265dd73cac8fe9c806afc74ec.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m+n$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n$:\n\n![](images/fe/fe7fb47997949a3bbf0699ee771a1a05f8c8d7c6558140719d7f7a00316fc231.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=4.5$ and $BH=2.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{81}{4}+\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{53}(m+n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502401 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c33297-8862-52ba-ae7e-117f940f7825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502324} {:answer/id #uuid "096e92bc-d7ac-5de6-9efd-fe57622569d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502327} {:answer/id #uuid "704b4538-66a1-56b4-a0be-0ab16e96992f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502364} {:answer/id #uuid "80148278-4eda-5d27-bc27-3f70e1ec97b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502370} {:answer/id #uuid "9fcd5af2-48b9-5a76-bea9-fec8bca5c287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fcd5af2-48b9-5a76-bea9-fec8bca5c287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502381} :answer-field/id #uuid "905b6f66-d160-5425-bc77-656eb54786d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502375}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c065984c-41d2-5c1b-a564-9053a81a79d9" :question/problem "![](images/92/92fcd6bef2b85d707fbe936c7aaa4870b64c158ca12f614123c0957dfa2a0efe.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m+n$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n$:\n\n![](images/39/39cc72f1b5da145c6c475c0759ab8df4bead1a136edadfae7c1e17291db451b1.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=1.5$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2+(2)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{5}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{5}(m+n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "050f0936-de36-51aa-be96-34bf22ff255b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502326} {:answer/id #uuid "145c7e10-0411-5226-b0b4-b88138b5fc49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{29}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502332} {:answer/id #uuid "24708689-ae25-5b89-9e77-19b9b6ff20fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{29}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502339} {:answer/id #uuid "3d56e48f-ff61-53aa-ba43-699f7f459463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502350} {:answer/id #uuid "77ace477-261c-5694-b9b7-bf4ec6f695ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24708689-ae25-5b89-9e77-19b9b6ff20fd" :answer/typ